   "description": "Vispo Systems delivers passive GPS-alternative navigation for contested environments. Its FPGA-based system harvests Doppler shifts from LEO satellite signals — such as Starlink — to compute real-time position and velocity without emitting any signal or relying on GPS infrastructure.\n\nBuilt on the same RF and FPGA foundation, Vispo also develops low-probability-of-intercept (LPI) mesh communications and passive RF sensing — forming a full electronic warfare toolkit for distributed unmanned platforms.",
   "founded": 2025,
   "headcount": "~10",
   "highlight": "Building Europe's first passive GPS-alternative navigation system — no GPS dependency, no signal emission, and no reliance on friendly infrastructure.",
